  "title": "Teams with no stragglers",
  "prompt": "A coach splits players into teams of a fixed size, in the order they are listed. If the last team would be too small, its players join the team before it instead, so nobody is left in a tiny team of their own.\n\nWrite `groupUp(items, size)` that takes an array of 0 to 25 whole numbers and a whole number `size` from 1 to 10, and returns an array of groups (arrays). Every group except the last has exactly `size` items; the last group has `size` or more items. The one exception is when there are fewer than `size` items in total: then there is a single group holding all of them. An empty array returns `[]`. The input must not be changed.\n\nExamples:\n\n- `groupUp([1,2,3,4,5,6,7], 3)` returns `[[1,2,3],[4,5,6,7]]`\n- `groupUp([1,2], 5)` returns `[[1,2]]`",
